<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Domingo Faustino Sarmiento</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1811–1888</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Domingo Faustino Sarmiento was an Argentine writer, educator and statesman who served as president from 1868 to 1874. An opponent of Rosas, he wrote Facundo in exile in Chile, a classic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American literature contrasting civilisation and barbarism. As president he expanded public schooling, encouraged immigration and carried out the first national <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a> in 1869.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/domingo-faustino-sarmiento.jpg" alt="Domingo Faustino Sarmiento" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarmiento.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
